WHAT: Final inliner tuning — raises max_inlinee_blocks 8→12, max_inlinee_insts
40→48, and adjusts the multi-block threshold for speed mode.

WHY: Last attempt to squeeze more inlining gains from threshold adjustments.

GAS IMPACT: -1193 gas total, mostly governance.
  governance/vote: -510
  governance/execute: -331
  governance/delegate: -238
  governance/propose: -199
  escrow/release: -48, deposit: -36
  governance/mint: -28
  Small regressions: math (+2), erc20/transfer (+10), groth16 (+196)

TEAM NOTES: The governance improvements come from inlining deeper into the
token contract's transfer/mint functions. The groth16 regression (+196) is
concerning — more aggressive inlining can increase code size and cause worse
instruction scheduling. This is the final commit in the campaign, and it
shows the characteristic mixed results of inliner tuning at its limits.

Campaign summary: 26 commits across sonatina and fe. The biggest wins came
from Fe std library changes (unchecked arithmetic, ArrayView), not from
sonatina optimizer tuning. Steps 15-18 (Fe std) saved ~12,000 gas vs
steps 1-14 (sonatina optimizer) saving ~1,500 gas.
